# Heavy or regenerable data — regenerate with pilot/scripts + phase1/scripts
# (see PILOT.md / phase1/README.md). NOTE: gitignore does not support inline comments.

# 4.2 GB of ChIP-Atlas bigWigs; re-fetch with pilot/scripts/03_download_bigwigs.sh
pilot/data/bigwigs/

# deepTools signal matrices + raw signal tables (large; regenerable via 04_quantify.py)
pilot/results/*.npz
pilot/results/*.tab

# Kept on purpose: all *.md, scripts, result *.png figures, *_summary.tsv,
# small manifests (manifest.tsv / selection.tsv / phase1_manifest.tsv), reference_regions.bed

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*~

# Phase 2 grid: keep the DECIDED grid (grid.20.bed) + manifests; ignore the regenerable
# comparison/diagnostic variants (stats live in phase2/PULL_DESIGN.md §8; rebuild via
# phase2/scripts/21_grid_from_persrx.sh). Raw per-SRX beds stay on Roihu scratch.
phase2/data/grid.bed
phase2/data/grid.10.bed
phase2/data/grid_seen_srx.txt

# Phase-2 pilot rehearsal: heavy regenerable matrices (regenerate via phase2/scripts/30_rehearse_local.sh
# CN=1 + phase2/score_pilot.py). Kept on purpose: the small *_summary.tsv + *.top_specific.tsv result tables.
phase2/rehearse/*.se_signal.tsv
phase2/rehearse/*.union_catalog.bed
phase2/rehearse/*.se_presence.tsv
phase2/rehearse/pilot_scores.jsd_*.tsv

# Phase-2 rehearsal logs (regenerable)
phase2/rehearse/*.log

# Phase-2 reference atlas (fetched off Roihu scratch 2026-07-22, scripts/50_fetch_and_clean.sh).
# The two SIGNAL matrices are 443 MB + 321 MB — over GitHub's 100 MB/file limit, and NOT
# regenerable without a ~43 BU re-pull, so they are protected by Dropbox + the 2 TB SSD copy,
# not by git. Everything else in phase2/results/ is small and IS tracked (catalogs, presence,
# s3norm params, failed_srx) — see phase2/results/README.md for the copy inventory.
phase2/results/atlas.se_signal.tsv.gz
phase2/results/atlas.s3.se_signal.tsv.gz

# Transient run logs (rsync progress etc.)
logs/

# Phase-2 scores: keep the SMALL canonical artifacts in git; the heavy dumps are regenerable via
# score_pilot.py (--dump-specific) and cn_ablation.py / concordance_bridge2.py — see phase2/scores/README.md.
# Line-level "specific" dumps (line is rankings-only, so a call set there is meaningless), the analytic
# level dumps (counts VOID, gotcha 71), and the analytic raw concordance pairs.
phase2/scores/*.line.specific.tsv.gz
phase2/scores/atlas.s3.Oncotree*.specific.tsv.gz
phase2/scores/atlas.s3.concordance2.pairs.tsv.gz

phase2/scores/*.rerun.log

# Machine-local configuration: real filesystem layout + HPC allocation id live ONLY here.
# `sample.env` is the tracked template. Never commit .env (gotcha 80).
.env
*.env
!sample.env

# Parsed-once caches (gene coordinates, ...) — regenerable, see secacts_env.cache_path()
.cache/

# Internal knowledge base: session handoff + the numbered gotchas log. Both are working
# documents that accrete local paths, private-memory links and notes on other projects, and
# neither is about using SE-CaCTS. They are for developing and maintaining the project, not for
# its readers. Kept on disk (Dropbox) for durability; deliberately never tracked.
nextsession.md
GOTCHAS.md
